[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Ordered finite control analyses and complex reporting

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
User-authorized work resumes after the completed hourly window; that schedule
remains paused. The target is the unchanged original ac-resistance.cir, with
all OP, AC and PZ operations and original assertions executed and compared.
Reuse the generated ANTLR grammar, existing typed requested analyses, bounded
PZ helper and bounded reporting evaluator. System.Numerics.Complex is the
standard-library numeric representation at this reporting boundary; no legacy
runtime or new expression parser enters the Rust engine. Existing independent
core/reuse decisions remain in force. RSpice's phase/plot semantics guide the
integration; its conformance smoke labels alone are not numerical evidence.

Plan: reproduce refusal in a public preparation test; add typed control PZ;
extend the one reporting evaluator with complex vectors and immutable
per-analysis input snapshots; admit only structurally unconditional finite
dispatch with reporting-only branches; connect all original analyses and
comparisons through the normal coordinator; verify full original assertions,
negative boundaries, reproducible properties, mutation and measured coverage.
Then independently diagnose and fix the original MOS memory startup and
waveforms, preserving original inputs and numerical comparison tolerances.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CONTROL-ORDERED-PLOTS-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Ordered finite dispatch with analysis-local vectors
STATEMENT: >>>
An admitted finite direct control program shall retain analysis order and
original source identities. Reporting after each analysis shall consume that
analysis's complete immutable voltage, branch-current and coordinate vectors,
never substitute another analysis plot or a selected probe. Unsupported
conditional dispatch, early exits affecting later analyses, loops around
analysis dispatch and unmodeled external effects shall be refused before
publishing a partial supported operation plan.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CONTROL-COMPLEX-VECTORS-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bounded complex reporting and scalar broadcasting
STATEMENT: >>>
The ordered reporting profile shall support finite complex AC vectors,
imaginary unit i, pi, arithmetic with scalar broadcasting, absolute magnitude,
real-vector maximum and bounded vector substitution. Shape mismatch,
nonfinite results, missing analysis snapshots and nonreal ordered comparisons
shall be explicit failures. Borrowed results shall not be mutated. The
existing real-only reporting API shall preserve its prior admission contract.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CONTROL-PZ-DISPATCH-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Typed control pole-zero request
STATEMENT: >>>
The generated control grammar shall retain PZ port spellings, voltage/current
transfer mode, pole/zero selection and original source range. Execution shall
reuse the qualified bounded PZ analysis and publish typed pole/zero vectors
for subsequent reporting, with explicit refusal outside its supported topology.
Independent ngspice comparison shall verify every requested root identity,
count and value without omitting original ordinary analyses or assertions.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-PARSER-EXECUTION-STACK-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Generated parser execution-stack resource boundary
STATEMENT: >>>
Generated recognition shall check runtime execution-stack headroom as well as
the fixed rule-depth bound. Insufficient headroom shall produce a structured
resource refusal without publishing partial syntax metadata or terminating
the process. Bounded control-expression recognition shall use the same guard.
Supported ordinary nesting shall remain covered by positive boundary tests;
the resource refusal is not a claim that arbitrarily deep valid syntax is
executable on every host stack.
<<<
